With a wand that early I would wish up my kit right away:

1. charging (duh)
2. SDSM (9-12 points of AC, reflection that will protect against
         monsters with wands)
3. AoLS (insurance)
*wait*
4. Sceptre of Might (MR, free hungerless conflict, honestly you
                     could have a worse melee weapon too)

As soon as max HP was 41, I would wish for the Sceptre of Might, and then
use the other wishes on... jumping boots, robe, marker? Maybe I would
just save them. Or wish for Grayswandir if I didn't have a longsword
yet; hell, why not. (The later point about Magicbane is a good one, but
twoweapon with Grayswandir is so broken I might just go with that.) If
I were super early in the game I would save a wish for another AoLS if
I needed it before I collected sleep resistance or something. You need
MR to protect you from:

 * death rays
 * polytraps
 * antimagic traps (yawn)
 * archliches and other big bad casters

The only one of these that can happen before you will have max HP 41 is
death rays, and reflection will protect you from those. You can wait for
MR until you have hit XL 5 or 6 as long as you don't go low enough to hit
polytraps (which can _cause_ archliches).  This would be my strategy for
any early wand for any character. For chaotics I would wish for a CoMR
instead of an MR-tifact, and if you are one of those "I don't wish for 
artifacts because blah blah justification I am hardcore" people, you can 
wish for a CoMR too. Same great taste, fewer free superpowers. 

